      "The relational gospel puts the weight on the first tense, because everything else flows from it. Growth is not climbing toward a new identity. It is unfolding the identity already given. Traditional theology often speaks of justification (instant) and sanctification (process); the relational view agrees with the shape but roots both in union with Christ rather than in a legal transaction followed by moral effort."
