      a: "That is a reasonable reading, and many commentators take it that way: the resurrection is the means or ground of the new birth that happens when believers come to faith. Peter is writing to believers (“us”), not making a statement about all humanity. The relational view argues that the ground and the event cannot be separated, since the new life we receive is Christ’s own risen life. But it should be honest that this is a theological inference, not the only possible reading of the verse."
